\section{FDR Sensitivity Analysis}
\label{sec:fdr_sensitivity}

Table~\ref{tab:fdr_sensitivity} reports the PermG forward significance counts under three correction standards. The consensus threshold $K{\geq}4/5$ used in the main text (Table~\ref{tab:generalization}) relies on raw permutation $p{<}0.05$, with cross-method agreement serving as multiplicity control.

